 :seed-or-trace "eacl-rust spec/10 §6.1 NEW-1; spec/12 §3.12 N1-N13"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :false-deny
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 pre-release before strong-Kleene fault semantics"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "Evidence composition was fault-dominant (a fault beat a Boolean absorber) and every route stopped at the first decisive operand, a fault included. The public outcome of a union with one faulting and one granting branch therefore depended on which branch a route evaluated first, a function of sealed rule ordinals, canonical node ids, entity ids, scan chunks, batch composition and route, not of the denotation. PR #209 pinned one such order."
 :fix
 "Composition is strong-Kleene and pointwise per completion of the residual Caveat atoms: a definite grant absorbs a fault in a union and a definite denial absorbs one in an intersection, an arrow or an exclusion, and a fault is never decisive, so every route keeps looking for an absorber. Recursion is the least fixed point in false < fault < true. The batched membership search no longer needs a fault-freedom certificate, and Caveated operands are no longer routed to ordered evaluation."
 :closing-evidence
